\,y=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-2)}{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $y$ into the equation of the paraboloid, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-2)}{2})}^{2} & =z+5 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{3(x-2)^{2}}{4} & =z+5 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}+4x+4}{4}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}-12x+12}{4} & =z+5 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}-8x+16}{4} & =z+5 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+4 & =z+5 \\\\ z & ={x}^{2}-2x-1 \\\\ z & =({x}^{2}-2x+1)-2 \\\\ z & ={(x-1)}^{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the vertex of the projection onto $xz$-plane is $(1,-2).$" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387905 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387906 13194139536187 true] [17592186387905 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387907 13194139536187 true] [17592186387905 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387908 13194139536187 true] [17592186387905 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387909 13194139536187 true] [17592186387905 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387910 13194139536187 true] [17592186387905 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536187 true] [17592186387905 1041 "selection" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387905 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387906 13194139536187 true] [17592186387905 1110 #uuid "e441e264-9702-5335-8ef0-7b56770206da" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387906 1034 "$(1,-2)$ in the $xz$-plane" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387906 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536187 true] [17592186387906 1111 #uuid "04fc3548-12a9-571b-9dd8-5ce4069c9ebc" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387907 1034 "$(-1,5)$ in the $xz$-plane" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387907 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536187 true] [17592186387907 1111 #uuid "c076f2c1-2c22-5ab8-b69c-93de4945e632" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387908 1034 "$(1,-5)$ in the $xz$-plane" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387908 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536187 true] [17592186387908 1111 #uuid "530613f5-a721-58c6-b989-a74c9746bc50" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387909 1034 "$(1,0)$ in the $xz$-plane" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387909 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536187 true] [17592186387909 1111 #uuid "66594093-3fff-546c-92b5-7a2493f8a697" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387910 1034 "$(-1,2)$ in the $xz$-plane" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387910 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536187 true] [17592186387910 1111 #uuid "179f9e7c-53eb-56e1-8d03-64d4037dcba7" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387911 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387912 13194139536187 true] [17592186387911 1089 "q-94784" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387911 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536187 true] [17592186387911 1100 "Find the point of the intersection of the elliptic cone $2{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}={z}^{2}$ and the line $x=y=\\frac{z+8}{2}.$" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387911 1113 #uuid "3dc5f127-8068-54c4-b54b-8ddcd406e234" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387911 1145 "First, we write the equation of our line in parametric form:\n\n$$\nx=y=\\frac{z+8}{2}=t\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}x=t \\\\ y=t \\\\ z=2t-8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSubstituting the above expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ 2{t}^{2}+2{t}^{2} & =(2t-8)^{2} \\\\ 4{t}^{2} & =4{t}^{2}-32t+64 \\\\ 32t & =64 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute our solution back into the equations of the line. For $t=2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2 \\\\ y=2 \\\\ z=2(2)-8=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(2,2,-4).$" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387913 13194139536187 true] [17592186387912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387914 13194139536187 true] [17592186387912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387915 13194139536187 true] [17592186387912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387916 13194139536187 true] [17592186387912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387917 13194139536187 true] [17592186387912 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536187 true] [17592186387912 1041 "selection" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387912 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387917 13194139536187 true] [17592186387912 1110 #uuid "7e5df432-e6e8-5c64-b25f-6e669ab6bb3e" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387913 1034 "$(-1,-1,-10)$  only" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387913 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536187 true] [17592186387913 1111 #uuid "0c54e040-0ada-51b6-8a72-999b584c38a1" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387914 1034 "$(3,3,-2)$  and $(-1,-1,-10)$" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387914 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536187 true] [17592186387914 1111 #uuid "878fa694-127c-5301-92f2-836789620487" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387915 1034 "$(-2,-2,-12)$   only" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387915 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536187 true] [17592186387915 1111 #uuid "20780e38-5285-5b15-a089-2423b26b1f13" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387916 1034 "$(1,1,-6)$  and $(2,2,-4)$" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387916 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536187 true] [17592186387916 1111 #uuid "24780450-ff62-53b1-ae6c-ca08f78d4459" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387917 1034 "$(2,2,-4)$ only" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387917 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536187 true] [17592186387917 1111 #uuid "e517a2b6-ffb3-59df-85a0-94ffce2ea96e" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387918 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387919 13194139536187 true] [17592186387918 1089 "q-94785" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387918 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536187 true] [17592186387918 1100 "Find the point of the intersection of the elliptic cone $2{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}=2{z}^{2}$ and the line $\\frac{x}{3}=y+1=\\frac{z}{3}.$" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387918 1113 #uuid "c7a9912a-e8fa-5a3a-bbb8-69d846d6c8b4" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387918 1145 "First, we write the equation of our line in the parametric form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{3}=y+1=\\frac{z}{3}=t\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}x=3t \\\\ y=t-1 \\\\ z=3t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSubstituting the above expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2} & =2{z}^{2} \\\\ 2(3t)^{2}+5(t-1)^{2} & =2(3t)^{2} \\\\ 5(t-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ (t-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ t-1 & =0 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute our solution back into the equations of the line. For $t=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3(1)=3 \\\\ y=1-1=0 \\\\ z=3(1)=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(3,0,3).$" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387919 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387920 13194139536187 true] [17592186387919 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387921 13194139536187 true] [17592186387919 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387922 13194139536187 true] [17592186387919 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387923 13194139536187 true] [17592186387919 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387924 13194139536187 true] [17592186387919 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536187 true] [17592186387919 1041 "selection" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387919 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387921 13194139536187 true] [17592186387919 1110 #uuid "197a9ca9-fe4b-5369-8cf1-14f9f99a8d49" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387920 1034 "$(-6,-3,-6)$ and $(3,0,3)$" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387920 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536187 true] [17592186387920 1111 #uuid "71e0555e-9121-5bcd-8612-c3317fc0555e" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387921 1034 "$(3,0,3)$ only" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387921 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536187 true] [17592186387921 1111 #uuid "2bf731e3-69c4-534f-aeee-e731635f07cf" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387922 1034 "$(-3,-2,-3)$  and $(0,-1,0)$" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387922 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536187 true] [17592186387922 1111 #uuid "1f240cb8-72c4-5baf-8a17-51b59f157fe9" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387923 1034 "$(0,-1,0)$ only" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387923 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536187 true] [17592186387923 1111 #uuid "26b26f6e-609a-5e13-8038-50053beecdd5" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387924 1034 "$(6,1,6)$ only" 13194139536187 true] [17592186387924 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536187 true] [1759218638